sucker-punches next big ps4 exclusive is  ghost of Tsushima a samurai action game  inspired by real world events but what  exactly is it here's everything you need  to know about the game so far the title  is a good place to start you are the  ghost in question fighting across the  very real Japanese island of Tsushima  the Mongol Empire invaded the island in  1274 and they succeeded in taking it  over ghosts of Tsushima takes place on  the occupied island with samurai jin  sekai fighting to retake his land from  the Mongols although the game has a  distinct Japanese setting it's worth  pointing out that you can play it in  both Japanese and English from the  recent story trailer it seems Jin's  fight won't always be an honorable one  as one character notes was nothing so  how exactly will you fight in ghosts of  Tsushima Sony's e3 2018 demo gives us a  good idea combat is slick and precise  with gin snapping quickly between  targeted foes to take them down  although jen has been trained as a  samurai he adopts a stealthy approach to  combat the invaders he uses tools like  ropes and arrows to give himself an  advantage over the brutal Mongol  soldiers combat changes based on how  many enemies you're facing in a fight  Tsushima also features a Dueling  component and sucker punch paid a lot of  attention to detail on each character's  sword Jin's weapon is a family heirloom  called the Sakai storm and it features  lightning bolts on its handguard the  same demo shows jen trading blows with  the female samurai Masako with a series  of fast-moving attacks and deflections  this duel is one of the game's side  stories the climax of a schism between  her and Jin sucker punch also draws  attention to the red leaves that fall  around the battle it considers these  swirling leaves a metaphor for the  team's work on the game like many ideas  bouncing around inside someone's head  jumping off the leaf metaphor it's  important to point out that ghosts of  Tsushima isn't all violent it's an  open-world game and the island is full  of natural beauty to take in as you ride  around on horseback as sucker-punch  studio head Chris Zimmerman puts it  quote this isn't a sea of enemies it's  more grounded than that there are times  when you're walking through the woods  and you listen to birds or  spook a deer or you hear a wolf in the  distance and then it pans across the  path and looks at you before it keeps  going that's kind of magical you can  experience that blend of vengeful  violence and natural beauty yourself  when ghosts of Tsushima comes to ps4 on  June 26 the standard edition will run  you sixty dollars us or 55 pounds but  you can also pick up the digital deluxe  edition for 70 bucks or 65 pounds that  includes the hero of Tsushima skin set  charm of Ho Chi Minh's favored one  technique point a ps4 dynamic theme  digital art book and director's  commentary the physical special edition  cost the same price and it includes the  same digital content via a PlayStation  Store voucher plus it comes with the  game in a steelbook case then there's  the collector's edition which will run  you a hundred and seventy dollars in the  u.s. you'll get all the same digital  content and the steelbook case plus a  replica mask sasha mona war banner for a  cheeky wrapping cloth physical art book  and a cloth world map for more  information on any of those editions hit  up GameSpot's pre-order guides for now  this has been everything you need to  know about ghosts of Tsushima so far  [Music]
 

